in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @uuid/spectral

# NOTE (Landing 4 soft-cascade, 2026-07-14): @spectral/signature (per
# Landing 2 docs/specs/gift-and-mirror-reflection.md §12) reads the
# visibility-filtered bauchladen at subject altitude, not at peer
# altitude. @bauchladen composition is subject-general per Landing 4
# (docs/specs/subject-bauchladen-visibility-and-eigenboard-loop.md
# e42181c); peer-scoped alias preserved for one release cycle per
# two-tick discipline.

# @spectral — the runtime namespace-parent.
#
# Shrunk 2026-07-01 per Loki §5 (Seam-ratified `17f0ee5`). @spectral
# was over-declared as a full family-root wearing BEAM-on-mirror
# operational-model ceremony; the shard's own "Substrate-already-had-
# the-word" section admitted its actual job:
#
#   "The parent was already implied by the path syntax; the family
#    root names it at the symbol altitude."
#
# That IS the namespace-parent signature. The operational surface
# (gen_prism, supervisor, parent, entanglement, registry, root — the
# BEAM analogues), the ouroboros pipeline, and the sibling-family
# candidates were narrative-in-a-header rather than substrate-decl at
# the family-root altitude. They live in `docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md`
# already (2026-06-10 spec; 20.3 KB); the species shards under
# `shards/spectral/` declare them at the substrate altitude when they
# land.
#
# === What @spectral IS now ===
#
# A namespace-parent for the runtime species living at
# `shards/spectral/<name>.mirror`. Path-container; no operational
# contract of its own. Sibling to @mirror, @kintsugi, @prism, @glass,
# @nl, @epistemologic, @facet, @io at the top-level path-altitude —
# but the sibling-family DISCIPLINES (form/process/shape/runtime, the
# ouroboros pipeline, gen_prism vocabulary) live at the SPECIES
# altitude, not here.
#
# === What @spectral was ===
#
# Recognition #46 second instance (2026-06-10): the substrate-pull
# cascade wanted a parent for `@spectral/db` (memory ref
# [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]; task #198) and
# `@spectral/garden` (task #118); path syntax already implied it; this
# shard names it. That job is DONE at namespace altitude.
#
# The BEAM-on-mirror operational model (gen_prism as gen_server
# analogue; supervisor/parent/entanglement/registry/root) is now
# documented at `docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md` and forward-promised
# as `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror`, `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`,
# `shards/spectral/parent.mirror`, `shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror`,
# `shards/spectral/registry.mirror`, `shards/spectral/root.mirror`.
# The ouroboros pipeline (substrate declarations → materialize → store
# → lens/unix → cargo → binary) lives in the spec; when the cycle
# closes, the closure is content-addressed, not header-narrative.
#
# === Species that gain @spectral as parent ===
#
#   @spectral/db          (existing; #198)
#   @spectral/garden      (existing; #118)
#   @spectral/portal      (runtime side of @mirror/spectral/portal)
#   @spectral/gen_prism   (forward-promised)
#   @spectral/supervisor  (forward-promised)
#   @spectral/parent      (forward-promised)
#   @spectral/entanglement (forward-promised)
#   @spectral/registry    (forward-promised)
#   @spectral/root        (forward-promised)
#
# === Path-syntax discipline ===
#
# @spectral sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass` per recognition #46
# (the path-syntax property); this namespace-parent itself uses
# `prism` per the depth-0 discipline. Sub-shards land at
# `shards/spectral/<name>.mirror`; deeper sub-shards at
# `shards/spectral/<group>/<name>.mirror`.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md` (the operational
#               spec — BEAM-on-mirror model, gen_prism surface,
#               supervision tree, entanglement graph, ouroboros
#               pipeline, bootstrap retirement),
#               `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` (the form-side
#               sibling family at @mirror/spectral),
#               `docs/specs/bootstrap-retirement-plan.md`.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]
#                      (the open foundation / closed engine
#                      business-model boundary; @mirror/store is
#                      open; @spectral/db is the engine on top),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the substrate had @spectral as a path-prefix
#                      before the family-root named it; this shrink
#                      admits the namespace-parent signature was the
#                      honest one all along).
# Related shards: mirror.mirror (sibling family root; the form-side
#                 of the substrate),
#                 kintsugi.mirror (sibling family root; the
#                 process-side transformation engine),
#                 mirror/spectral.mirror (the SHAPE — orchestra
#                 observation surface at the form altitude;
#                 species under @spectral are the RUNTIME the score
#                 observes),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the runtime state surface
#                 carrier; gen_prism state — when it lands — is a
#                 shard ref into @mirror/store).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/spectral.mirror`
# declares `@spectral` as the namespace-parent; species live at
# `shards/spectral/<name>.mirror`.

out @spectral
